# What does NOT go into the build context.
#
# Two reasons this matters beyond upload speed. A stray `.env.local` in the
# context would be copied by `COPY . .` and would then OVERRIDE
# `.env.production`, so the image would quietly be built against whatever a
# developer last pointed their laptop at — a localhost API in a production
# image, with nothing failing. And `node_modules` from a Windows machine holds
# native binaries for the wrong platform, which `npm ci` in the build stage must
# be allowed to replace rather than inherit.

# Installed fresh inside the image, for linux/amd64.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — produced by the build stage, never copied in.
dist
dist-ssr
*.tsbuildinfo

# ⚠ Developer env overrides. `.env.production` is deliberately NOT listed here:
#   it is the configuration this image is built from.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.test

# History and tooling that the build never reads.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.nyc_output

# Documentation and the API contract mirror. ~1 MB of markdown that no build
# step opens; excluded so the context stays small and cache keys stay stable.
api-doc
*.md
!README.md

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
